  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on skewness, which—in this binary-outcome context—aligns with assigning higher probability to a favorable outcome. Lottery A has a higher probability (0.2% vs 0.1%) of a non-zero result, so the reason would prefer A. The individual also chooses A and bases the decision on the higher probability of winning. While the individual does not use the term 'skewness' or demonstrate an analysis of distribution shape, the informational basis of the decision (probability of favorable outcome) matches the relevant information for the decision reason. The justification—favoring higher probability of gain—coincides with the rule implied by the reason in this specific case. Although the individual likely lacks a technical understanding of skewness, the cognitive process aligns with the operational outcome of the reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used a reasoning pattern consistent with the decision reason, even if not articulated as such.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
